/**
 * ApiPage.tsx
 * ------------
 * The API management page of the Underpeaks console.
 * Located at: /console/api
 *
 * What does this page do?
 * ------------------------
 * It gives developers a full view of the API layer that Underpeaks automatically
 * generates from your CMS models, plus tools to manage API keys and test endpoints.
 *
 * The page is split into three tabs:
 *
 *  1. Endpoints tab
 *     Shows all auto-generated REST endpoints (created automatically from your models)
 *     and any custom endpoints you have added. Includes search and filter controls,
 *     and each endpoint row can be expanded to see example requests and run a test.
 *
 *  2. API Keys tab
 *     Lists all API keys for the project. Keys can be revealed, copied, or deleted.
 *     New keys can be generated by entering a name and clicking Generate.
 *
 *  3. Reference tab
 *     Static documentation showing all supported query parameters, filter operators,
 *     and a full worked example of a complex API query.
 *
 * What are "auto" vs "custom" endpoints?
 * ----------------------------------------
 * - Auto endpoints are generated automatically by Underpeaks for every model you create.
 *   For example, if you have a "Products" model, Underpeaks generates GET, POST, PUT,
 *   and DELETE endpoints for it automatically — no code required.
 * - Custom endpoints are written by you (or your developers) to contain business logic
 *   that goes beyond simple CRUD — for example, creating an order, sending a confirmation
 *   email, and decrementing stock all in one API call.
 *
 * ⚠️  Security notes:
 *   - API key generation MUST be moved to the server before production (see createKey TODO)
 *   - Full API key values are held in component state — they should only be fetched
 *     from the server when the user explicitly reveals them, not stored in the UI
 */

